Statement: "Redeploying release 2.3 is a complete rollback plan for release 2.4."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. Redeploying 2.3 brings back code that reads and writes submissions.score, but the migration has already renamed the column, so every 2.3 query fails with "column score does not exist". The same failure happens during the forward rollout: the migration runs first, and the 2.3 pods that are still serving traffic break until the deploy finishes. A code rollback does not undo a schema change. A safe plan uses expand and contract: add points, write both columns, backfill, switch reads to points, and drop score in a later release, so that at every step both the old and the new code can run and each step has its own rollback. The misconception is that "revert the deploy" undoes a release; it undoes only the code, never the data or the schema.', 2, 5
